  "notes": "Cash basis. Same choices as FY2023/FY2024: the Sewer fund column of the governmental funds statements is recorded as business-type (cash measure, 390,838 -> 671,524, p4); governmental totals and fund balances are the Total Governmental column minus the Sewer column; Licenses, fees, and permits split by fund column; Sewer cash in bank and restricted fund balance tagged business-type. Statement lines from the Total Governmental column (p4). The statement's Intergovernmental 97,837 includes the General Fund Street department's Motor vehicle fees 15,577 (the General Fund column 97,204 = Motor vehicle fees 15,577 + Intergovernmental 81,627 on the departmental schedule p6), so it is split (split_from). Balances are printed as fund balance (cash basis), so beginning/ending_fund_balance are filled; cash fields left null as in later years (governmental cash would have to be derived from the Total column minus Sewer; Total column ending cash in bank 4,147,025, cash with county treasurer 18,716 and certificates of deposit 200,305 are on the balance sheet p3). No transfers or debt proceeds printed (transfers line nil). Balance sheet from the Statement of Fund Balances - Governmental Funds Total column (equals the government-wide Statement of Net Position, p1). Detail: General Fund from the combining schedule by department (p6, one line per department column); Keno, TIF, Debt Service and Capital Projects statement-column detail not added (as in FY2023/FY2024). The all-funds budget schedule (p5) is not recorded, to avoid double counting. Read pages 1-6 of 6"
}
